  'Branding and Identity Design',
  'Branding and Identity Design is an advanced Year 3 studio course in logos, brand systems, and visual identity. Students learn to connect strategy, research, positioning, verbal identity, marks, typography, color, imagery, guidelines, applications, and implementation into a coherent identity system. The course is designed for graphic design students preparing for senior studio, portfolio review, internships, and professional client work. It balances strategic brand thinking with rigorous visual craft, critique, systems documentation, ethical judgment, accessibility, and real-world presentation.',
  $brndjson${"slug": "branding-and-identity-design", "title": "Branding and Identity Design", "description": "Branding and Identity Design is an advanced Year 3 studio course in logos, brand systems, and visual identity. Students learn to connect strategy, research, positioning, verbal identity, marks, typography, color, imagery, guidelines, applications, and implementation into a coherent identity system. The course is designed for graphic design students preparing for senior studio, portfolio review, internships, and professional client work. It balances strategic brand thinking with rigorous visual craft, critique, systems documentation, ethical judgment, accessibility, and real-world presentation.", "topics": [{"id": "114d617c-1e8e-478d-bd14-eca555f2a30a", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Strategy, Purpose, and Positioning", "description": "This opening topic frames identity design as strategic communication, not surface styling. Students learn to connect visual decisions to purpose, audience, differentiation, and organizational behavior.", "children": [{"id": "617093e8-8e55-4421-9162-f184aa0d8342", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purpose and promise", "children": [{"id": "82b63b1a-ae5d-4078-ad56-a08fc50cb977", "type": "concept", "title": "Mission, vision, and values"}, {"id": "ae0fd519-2737-4f4d-880f-a065fe380915", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand promise and proof points"}, {"id": "2f4c26f2-7948-4cac-92a1-9bf6b3882935", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder expectations"}], "description": "Students clarify what the brand exists to do and what expectation it creates for people."}, {"id": "fde34a7b-b7fb-4fd0-bc43-6f759c6b1b0d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Positioning", "children": [{"id": "a3e7ac7f-1ad8-4bf3-ae0d-a5726b2dedd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Category frame and competitors"}, {"id": "0b127225-f8d0-435b-939c-f2f5604eeef9", "type": "concept", "title": "Points of parity and difference"}, {"id": "ff505662-6325-4b5b-8beb-4950506c8d7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Positioning statements"}], "description": "The point is to define a credible place in the audience's mind before designing assets."}, {"id": "bc1652b7-bb22-44ea-bb65-3698df051ae9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative criteria", "children": [{"id": "5024ea10-0e0b-48cb-8313-b36b5527d12f", "type": "concept", "title": "Design objectives"}, {"id": "6fc30b47-5f1f-4853-9d2a-01479aaee02f", "type": "concept", "title": "Success criteria"}, {"id": "794a9c9d-08c0-4f78-ad74-99968455f853", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraints and opportunities"}], "description": "Students turn strategy into design requirements that can guide critique and revision."}]}, {"id": "04c127bc-403c-492a-83c0-032dc1ae1b9a", "type": "topic", "title": "Audience Research, Cultural Context, and Insight", "description": "This section teaches students to design from evidence and empathy. Strong identity work begins by understanding people, context, category codes, and cultural meaning.", "children": [{"id": "a6d28452-cf5d-4f64-940b-811ad5b53eae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience discovery", "children": [{"id": "2d685f8a-1d26-4d1b-ad67-43ee99d1491d", "type": "concept", "title": "Personas and need states"}, {"id": "d95d65e7-33b5-4f7a-835a-1f50390c2aa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews and observation"}, {"id": "83c847ff-77e5-4223-8bed-3852395ea37b", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience language and behavior"}], "description": "Students learn to gather useful information about the people a brand needs to serve."}, {"id": "b8915ac0-ff6f-4acc-8f11-f3c3eb4d03d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitive and category audit", "children": [{"id": "5c601996-81e7-47a7-a601-7bcbcb595d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Category conventions"}, {"id": "b64927c7-9658-4b1c-b02b-9e167e490c23", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual sameness and white space"}, {"id": "2c0c8f22-ad30-4e00-a471-de86849a38a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Benchmarking and mood boards"}], "description": "The gist is to see what already exists before deciding how to stand apart."}, {"id": "fd4ffc54-406d-4d32-b4b8-6b142c0af2ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Insight synthesis", "children": [{"id": "b851f1e4-332e-4c29-8a6f-b883b719842c", "type": "concept", "title": "Patterns and tensions"}, {"id": "e2922867-4387-4382-bb69-de05fc1855f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Design implications"}, {"id": "4f3da21c-57bb-4a13-be45-11a07a8df107", "type": "concept", "title": "Research-backed creative brief"}], "description": "Students turn messy research into focused opportunities for design action."}]}, {"id": "9b9bf243-366b-4cec-9e47-578ef9502a31", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Equity, Architecture, and Portfolio Logic", "description": "Identity systems often live inside larger brand structures. This topic introduces brand value, hierarchy, sub-brands, extensions, and portfolio clarity.", "children": [{"id": "2dfde21f-4d26-4e38-a202-3dc7457ccfe7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brand equity", "children": [{"id": "460bed79-0432-4b4c-a6e5-741046855afa", "type": "concept", "title": "Awareness and associations"}, {"id": "a13ad644-13a8-47b2-b762-f936c0bf0557", "type": "concept", "title": "Perceived quality and loyalty"}, {"id": "38ac49d5-f544-4708-9fb0-58f8af296574", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental and physical availability"}], "description": "Students learn how recognition, associations, trust, and experience create value over time."}, {"id": "778a81f3-9ea5-4526-a2fa-84823fb5b131", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Architecture models", "children": [{"id": "9586d957-ca14-4a63-97ab-e13c1911eb56", "type": "concept", "title": "Branded house"}, {"id": "3b7ab269-f122-4c08-9b91-fa143097f49e", "type": "concept", "title": "House of brands"}, {"id": "119c5b03-b622-4ba2-bbe3-0005eb4cf495", "type": "concept", "title": "Endorsed and hybrid systems"}], "description": "The point is to choose relationships that make sense to customers and organizations."}, {"id": "70ed3745-f3ad-41ae-80be-92343912760a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio decisions", "children": [{"id": "3ba8c315-635b-442c-8b74-b6dc5645a86d", "type": "concept", "title": "Product families"}, {"id": "97c6db9a-36d0-43c3-9aee-a569f035c16f", "type": "concept", "title": "Sub-brand roles"}, {"id": "c1be5b9a-c678-4a94-9bfe-433b863b61f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration and governance"}], "description": "Students consider when to extend, consolidate, rename, or separate identities."}]}, {"id": "1a370895-75c9-4f45-9fcf-67ee604c18e0", "type": "topic", "title": "Naming, Verbal Identity, Voice, and Tone", "description": "Brand identity is both visual and verbal. Students learn to shape names, taglines, message hierarchy, and tone so language and design feel like one system.", "children": [{"id": "a0e6bcff-61a0-4f3c-8dea-9272f4b9e677", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Naming strategy", "children": [{"id": "7aefeec3-17d7-496e-89cd-225cb6bc1aab", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, evocative, coined, and founder names"}, {"id": "d6b7b236-947f-4959-933f-168305e924c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening and shortlisting"}, {"id": "1125fab8-6003-401e-8bda-a19c71e234b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Trademark and domain awareness"}], "description": "The point is to generate names that are memorable, usable, ownable, and strategically aligned."}, {"id": "6537988f-1021-4e7e-8a86-6834285c4b15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voice and tone", "children": [{"id": "387b578e-f6be-4d2d-8379-816ec27f9fad", "type": "concept", "title": "Personality attributes"}, {"id": "154860c2-eb43-4239-a793-820d330ea9de", "type": "concept", "title": "Tone range by context"}, {"id": "f78f2e8e-e693-4c69-b14c-305b47d76d0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Do and do not examples"}], "description": "Students define how the brand sounds in different situations without becoming inconsistent."}, {"id": "065cbeb2-cba1-4c99-b016-fb9d9ff58c90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Messaging system", "children": [{"id": "eb48acc0-8b49-4cd0-a295-16dc00542201", "type": "concept", "title": "Taglines and value propositions"}, {"id": "e41fd282-83d2-4a96-9fe1-3f54866f5044", "type": "concept", "title": "Message pillars"}, {"id": "3829757e-8b91-4a3e-a5be-6625c995382d", "type": "concept", "title": "Proof points and calls to action"}], "description": "Students learn to structure claims and stories for multiple audiences and channels."}]}, {"id": "a586efba-dff3-4722-a31d-e779632b68c4", "type": "topic", "title": "Logo Design, Marks, Wordmarks, and Symbol Systems", "description": "This studio core develops disciplined mark-making. Students move from sketches to refined logos that are distinctive, scalable, flexible, and strategically justified.", "children": [{"id": "c7e2c172-7aec-4208-9ab5-3a62e6ed515c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept development", "children": [{"id": "0d31d479-f83a-4396-b5ed-60c6110c671d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sketching and ideation"}, {"id": "4486b7e8-1d8a-4a96-8091-b5948a5d1d2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Metaphor and abstraction"}, {"id": "c71c602f-20eb-4eea-954a-0eaacad5e9c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept selection criteria"}], "description": "Students learn to generate many routes before committing to one polished direction."}, {"id": "badaf466-b963-479f-92b0-54f3fa1227e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logo construction", "children": [{"id": "dfd6aaef-3869-4878-8616-999091062304", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometry and optical correction"}, {"id": "262b4b85-dddf-4483-9465-38a2a4bc0c3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative space"}, {"id": "5b834345-fe69-4b01-8433-b68cee2e9f97", "type": "concept", "title": "Lockups and clear space"}], "description": "The gist is to refine form so the mark works technically and perceptually."}, {"id": "4b53f474-aa27-46b1-93a4-1b53f09b1a19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing and refinement", "children": [{"id": "d4a13058-63d9-4b34-9b5b-9fdfc108e4f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-size performance"}, {"id": "473195a0-6f3d-478d-8c45-0c031db670f8", "type": "concept", "title": "One-color and reverse use"}, {"id": "64e3678f-ba44-41e4-80f2-290282ed75a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Confusability and memorability"}], "description": "Students learn to stress-test marks before finalizing them."}]}, {"id": "00bc6dc8-149e-426a-9da1-cb5b48dfe0da", "type": "topic", "title": "Typography for Identity Systems", "description": "Typography carries personality, hierarchy, and usability. This topic teaches students to choose and use type as a strategic brand voice across print and digital contexts.", "children": [{"id": "b00fcc47-2e64-48ae-95e6-9c6265ec433b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Typeface selection", "children": [{"id": "dd4038a1-2d8e-43de-9bfa-4dee2376ebf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Classification and personality"}, {"id": "157bc803-2087-4fcf-89b3-01c616977ffb", "type": "concept", "title": "Licensing and availability"}, {"id": "e5529add-0b96-4d45-bfe9-e25bc65e05d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Variable fonts and digital use"}], "description": "Students learn to match type choices to strategy, audience, and implementation reality."}, {"id": "522e7d4b-c9dd-4dea-abca-70bf689416ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Typographic system", "children": [{"id": "c0577c32-7edf-414f-81f9-3382ef775ed0", "type": "concept", "title": "Display, text, and UI roles"}, {"id": "f32760d1-13a8-4755-8824-827d512752a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale, spacing, and grids"}, {"id": "64893252-ae01-4952-b3fe-879734e1006b", "type": "concept", "title": "Language support and accessibility"}], "description": "The point is to create hierarchy and rhythm that can scale across many assets."}, {"id": "9bd9f9d3-bce8-4fee-bfa7-228c8f745832", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Custom type and lettering", "children": [{"id": "9a31de74-931d-44ca-b0fa-a3ddf5bf60ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Letterform refinement"}, {"id": "8d9cb9c4-4cef-4b6c-950f-79ee65445301", "type": "concept", "title": "Optical balance"}, {"id": "a2ffb352-4d7f-4997-8d5e-c7f2c7ff1160", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency with the broader system"}], "description": "Students explore when a custom wordmark or type modification is worth the effort."}]}, {"id": "872eb134-a700-47b7-9763-7697e26e9e03", "type": "topic", "title": "Color, Form, Image, and Graphic Language", "description": "A brand becomes recognizable through repeated visual behavior. Students build palettes, forms, imagery, icons, patterns, and compositional rules that support a coherent identity.", "children": [{"id": "6b9c67bb-59ea-4e6a-aa7f-3b261f54d7dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color systems", "children": [{"id": "e882f3b1-e1ee-4292-887e-b91537037901", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary palettes"}, {"id": "e19ccf2c-b7a6-4df7-a352-88644f5b90af", "type": "concept", "title": "CMYK, RGB, HEX, Pantone, and accessibility"}, {"id": "a6f004d6-17cf-4f34-8564-6e5824ab9432", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and color roles"}], "description": "Students learn to make palettes that are expressive, accessible, and reproducible."}, {"id": "79244f38-7573-40f7-a5f4-3935de47364d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Graphic elements", "children": [{"id": "7893b07a-0e61-4a1a-a35a-eacec872b3cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Patterns and shapes"}, {"id": "f75c7dcf-6f11-41ab-9b2d-5bb4e3486a33", "type": "concept", "title": "Icon and illustration styles"}, {"id": "37d3c170-de81-4037-88cf-1637c375fa12", "type": "concept", "title": "Photography and art direction"}], "description": "The point is to create useful design ingredients beyond the logo."}, {"id": "43ad39e2-fa87-45ae-902b-21e50dbc6ff2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual consistency", "children": [{"id": "260b789c-1461-4671-895b-68b6dfc9a02d", "type": "concept", "title": "Motifs and signature moves"}, {"id": "ef498e18-41fc-4860-90a9-f22ab2d7a412", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules for variation"}, {"id": "1ce80ca3-fca5-42ac-aff7-a1d4da20e5a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding sameness and clutter"}], "description": "Students learn how repetition and variation create a living system."}]}, {"id": "9a8f8697-c7d5-459e-9a96-5161277d89ee", "type": "topic", "title": "Identity Systems, Grid Logic, and Design Principles", "description": "This topic shifts students from individual deliverables to systems thinking. A strong identity creates rules that other designers can use without weakening the brand.", "children": [{"id": "d4f352db-d1d2-4a01-b7bc-153f0d54cc74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "System principles", "children": [{"id": "95de0735-1d0d-4086-8ef8-11ace8e25349", "type": "concept", "title": "Core design principles"}, {"id": "6088aaf6-e852-4138-a134-7b7a2997502a", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible versus fixed elements"}, {"id": "ad721b06-8fe8-4bb8-bde1-eba9ceb39fc2", "type": "concept", "title": "System boundaries"}], "description": "Students identify the few rules that make the identity recognizable."}, {"id": "6241c5da-c9ff-4317-be2d-6e5667ab6eba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layout and grid logic", "children": [{"id": "dfd75409-3311-4d45-baf1-b4db97b71571", "type": "concept", "title": "Grid structures"}, {"id": "60d64b77-3d84-47e1-8f4c-2b05bba369f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Spacing and proportion"}, {"id": "1e4c162a-49b5-4fc3-8205-eae157ac0929", "type": "concept", "title": "Modular layouts"}], "description": "The gist is to make applications feel related even across different formats."}, {"id": "925681d6-0736-4be9-a83b-a69cb1d9347d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scalability", "children": [{"id": "3311689a-fd1b-4aaa-a750-d30eaa0eba47", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset families"}, {"id": "fe257c50-24f5-4871-b6fe-a06768e11246", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates and variants"}, {"id": "824172d9-7142-44a3-97e1-febc77684670", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth without fragmentation"}], "description": "Students learn to design for both small assets and complex campaigns."}]}, {"id": "fdb7a787-78ee-4529-8f69-d725102fb469", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Applications Across Touchpoints", "description": "Identity design becomes real through use. Students apply the system across varied touchpoints and learn to adjust while preserving recognizability.", "children": [{"id": "d856abcc-c877-49c9-9623-5ff984c0908d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Print and packaging", "children": [{"id": "d24226b6-2833-4c64-82a0-4ed2c4049453", "type": "concept", "title": "Stationery and collateral"}, {"id": "57421bfa-beb8-471f-bd72-7e8de394a893", "type": "concept", "title": "Packaging hierarchy"}, {"id": "cebbdf86-9233-48ce-af60-b24144d2953d", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials, finishes, and print constraints"}], "description": "Students practice translating identity into tangible, production-aware formats."}, {"id": "3f191904-3b14-445f-8436-5ff49042ecb2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital and social", "children": [{"id": "80cd95f7-05d7-42f2-a7d5-08a6087bec9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Social templates"}, {"id": "fe48757e-7a16-4857-8536-a9bab7e9dc07", "type": "concept", "title": "Web and mobile assets"}, {"id": "2be07a82-4ffe-4ae6-81bb-20885a71f235", "type": "concept", "title": "Thumbnails, avatars, and responsive marks"}], "description": "The point is to create brand behavior for fast-moving, screen-based contexts."}, {"id": "0416aeac-9c44-44f8-8334-700ff029901d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spatial and experiential", "children": [{"id": "43cc0e25-0a10-4bfe-963e-2e131d080803", "type": "concept", "title": "Signage and wayfinding"}, {"id": "42b996f7-116e-45a9-896f-6faa7d02e7b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Events and retail"}, {"id": "0d5a439f-98e8-4e3c-965c-d770e7d358ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental graphics"}], "description": "Students consider how identity functions in environments and public interactions."}]}, {"id": "ba2dd522-f3f3-43f8-a298-60c0a2e234b3", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Brand Systems, UI Components, and Accessibility", "description": "Modern identities must work inside interfaces and design systems. Students learn how brand choices become tokens, components, states, and accessible experiences.", "children": [{"id": "706c5358-1fae-4980-a5bf-84e8da32d9a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design tokens", "children": [{"id": "a7127c51-7ce8-42e8-94f3-23ef20ceae0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Color tokens"}, {"id": "6ad56203-5591-4c4d-ae4c-01c783703b20", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography tokens"}, {"id": "c10ec19b-194f-495c-b8db-b674fd3c01f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Spacing, radius, and elevation rules"}], "description": "Students translate brand choices into maintainable digital variables."}, {"id": "adb8dffc-6a13-4687-8a81-bdb93cba1501", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UI components", "children": [{"id": "37544481-c2c8-4822-ad23-4086cacf7ca5", "type": "concept", "title": "Buttons, forms, cards, and navigation"}, {"id": "5b0f0e7d-2450-4bc5-b771-c7e833349c30", "type": "concept", "title": "States and feedback"}, {"id": "820243a3-1730-4cd8-825e-842d0fbcd92b", "type": "concept", "title": "Component documentation"}], "description": "The point is to preserve brand expression while supporting usability."}, {"id": "e5aeadba-d525-4089-991c-09e75604f3be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility", "children": [{"id": "faea7fb3-fe7f-4d73-b263-9275c42c8f80", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and color blindness"}, {"id": "a9786468-f263-428b-8437-5581b196aea5", "type": "concept", "title": "Readable type and motion sensitivity"}, {"id": "893f066c-a9f1-4391-92aa-e8d5f427fa38", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and semantic handoff"}], "description": "Students learn that brand consistency cannot override legibility, contrast, or inclusive use."}]}, {"id": "6a563e2c-046b-4940-8267-0371dea6c5ab", "type": "topic", "title": "Motion, Sound, and Experiential Brand Behavior", "description": "Identity increasingly lives in time. This topic introduces motion, interaction, and sensory behavior as part of the brand system.", "children": [{"id": "739e7946-1940-4375-adfc-e0ed309e0000", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motion principles", "children": [{"id": "2f28d55b-c9ef-4291-9379-f1717d7ae4cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Timing and easing"}, {"id": "2f2f9c46-5832-4dbb-a18f-8e8b7bc95c2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions and reveals"}, {"id": "7f007148-f158-4b6b-830e-bea5374c032c", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion personality"}], "description": "Students define how a brand moves so animation supports identity rather than decoration."}, {"id": "4635d434-415e-4db9-9ca5-181828c5647c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interactive behavior", "children": [{"id": "974b8395-463d-4723-82d5-245d3cf3599f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hover, tap, loading, and feedback states"}, {"id": "b336d449-7ee6-4f38-b6f7-2c93361d1c3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Microinteractions"}, {"id": "af875f28-9905-45b0-b986-b241722973df", "type": "concept", "title": "Error and success moments"}], "description": "The gist is to make brand expression responsive to user action."}, {"id": "fbaae073-8b29-4121-80a4-8ad2bcf0968d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensory extensions", "children": [{"id": "c232d113-f96a-4ded-acbb-da6d0e61d10d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sonic logos and cues"}, {"id": "8b845924-2f0d-4255-9db8-10d4c9c72869", "type": "concept", "title": "Event experience"}, {"id": "28bcf86d-1b67-4693-b746-fb2bf55c3c39", "type": "concept", "title": "Multisensory consistency"}], "description": "Students consider sound, haptics, and experience design where appropriate."}]}, {"id": "d136ea02-b4ea-475f-9259-ba27a43061b1", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Guidelines, Asset Libraries, and Governance", "description": "Guidelines turn design into implementation. Students learn to document rules, rationale, files, and examples so a brand can be used by many people without falling apart.", "children": [{"id": "68ae7928-aea6-4188-9538-fe49fa5f2f93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Guideline structure", "children": [{"id": "e0dbfc83-914a-4790-a7b2-b1c4b98c3f5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo rules"}, {"id": "9cd3c432-4a98-43af-b69f-7b708a8955fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, type, image, and layout standards"}, {"id": "fb9d9a54-2ddf-40e6-bbec-ea00182c1cbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice, examples, and rationale"}], "description": "Students learn what a useful brand guide must explain."}, {"id": "be3fbc0d-1a96-4b92-a5e5-de22f0dcb1be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Asset management", "children": [{"id": "700e79e0-a02f-462c-8f37-4b9b8236cd6d", "type": "concept", "title": "File formats and naming"}, {"id": "ba1e0bc3-8aa2-4798-a6e6-7557dda2de83", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates and libraries"}, {"id": "de03e424-1657-451c-a63c-f2abdcedc952", "type": "concept", "title": "Version control"}], "description": "The point is to package files so teams can actually use them correctly."}, {"id": "bb5eb2ba-9ef3-42a6-bb80-2d472297a5ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance", "children": [{"id": "4a1cc187-5351-4a4c-91f3-823979c3595a", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval workflows"}, {"id": "bad6063f-981d-4104-97f1-5ae0703a597a", "type": "concept", "title": "Use cases and exceptions"}, {"id": "d6ea9161-c9be-4736-b6a9-5f280802c264", "type": "concept", "title": "Training and stewardship"}], "description": "Students consider how brands are maintained after launch."}]}, {"id": "bdd2a980-ecfa-4d64-aac0-8f7b7b1b0fd4", "type": "topic", "title": "Rebranding, Refreshes, and Identity Migration", "description": "Rebranding is not a blank slate. Students learn to preserve useful equity, diagnose real problems, and manage change across audiences and touchpoints.", "children": [{"id": "67cb9ff3-eea7-4b24-ac3f-765b5b8897c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brand audit", "children": [{"id": "be0c7acc-46ae-4f6d-b02a-493d2a506071", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity inventory"}, {"id": "ee9b2c59-02aa-477e-ba1a-d3e2e1403983", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder interviews"}, {"id": "91e89594-b0a9-4a67-8d4f-fdeb8cde217e", "type": "concept", "title": "Touchpoint and consistency audit"}], "description": "Students evaluate what should be kept, repaired, retired, or amplified."}, {"id": "96286f26-8a87-4c4e-a35b-b3a195c68444", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Redesign strategy", "children": [{"id": "fe0c1adc-57a9-43b4-afa6-b4ab768257fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Refresh versus rebrand"}, {"id": "c8012d39-0426-4c65-b170-93dfeda7a2a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration risk"}, {"id": "5187a235-a128-4c40-9bee-33a15e69473f", "type": "concept", "title": "Launch narrative"}], "description": "The gist is to decide the degree of change before changing the visuals."}, {"id": "d386d1b2-eddd-49c6-80de-159474fe97d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation planning", "children": [{"id": "fe3d2a43-2d65-4b54-8dc1-c932b8e6b91f", "type": "concept", "title": "Phased rollout"}, {"id": "976353ba-bf1b-498e-b8fd-469f6871c2a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Old-to-new asset mapping"}, {"id": "c9a8e61b-7f2b-4dcd-96ae-1494c8fbcf51", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal adoption and training"}], "description": "Students learn how a redesign rolls out in the real world."}]}, {"id": "fded4907-249c-4a99-b179-6dd19ecbec7a", "type": "topic", "title": "Global, Local, Inclusive, and Ethical Branding", "description": "This topic asks students to design with cultural intelligence and responsibility. Identity work can include, exclude, inspire, confuse, stereotype, or repair trust.", "children": [{"id": "4dc933a5-d76e-4a55-a431-59a613b9e527", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural meaning", "children": [{"id": "3927abbb-9f5a-4e20-8340-d14097af91b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Localization and translation"}, {"id": "5b6d2934-863d-4bc6-8be7-bd2797f57920", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural codes and taboos"}, {"id": "b3fa1ed7-e920-4827-aaa6-86634d834ee0", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding appropriation and stereotypes"}], "description": "Students learn to research symbols, colors, language, and imagery across contexts."}, {"id": "12a6b64e-8f73-4118-9398-3cb2cffa212d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive identity", "children": [{"id": "8ac9b265-4425-44b0-9e04-d55420ca27b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and imagery"}, {"id": "a42c6bfe-a814-4e33-8759-95ea04ad4765", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility as identity quality"}, {"id": "9463d3d1-58ce-405e-8b73-727b68ea1896", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive naming and language"}], "description": "The point is to consider who is represented, who can use the system, and who may be harmed."}, {"id": "43bfb301-ed42-405e-90a2-e1904eb4ff32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical practice", "children": [{"id": "e8010bef-abaa-4568-9b87-6b7a294384ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Greenwashing and authenticity"}, {"id": "bffd38fc-a717-458f-ae17-233cfd31f4fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Dark patterns and manipulation"}, {"id": "e13b7d28-3300-4ec6-816d-6448dfcfebc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency and accountability"}], "description": "Students connect design choices to social, environmental, and reputational consequences."}]}, {"id": "7046f2b4-1555-444f-bcb6-8de247c86645", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Measurement, Testing, and Critique", "description": "Identity systems should be judged by more than taste. Students learn to evaluate recognition, clarity, usability, distinctiveness, fit, and audience response.", "children": [{"id": "de03487c-0170-4f79-a617-66ad9d6f64fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Qualitative testing", "children": [{"id": "50e7370d-0dda-4178-a5ef-c6d79c2baedc", "type": "concept", "title": "Perception interviews"}, {"id": "cfea8f3e-9c4b-4205-b46e-a707001b8497", "type": "concept", "title": "Preference versus fit"}, {"id": "65822adc-d14c-4ae3-ba57-7d5c901f50fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique protocols"}], "description": "Students use critique and user feedback to identify strengths and problems."}, {"id": "cbc68ef3-6fdf-4f69-b50c-b30ab77ccb66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quantitative indicators", "children": [{"id": "65f581e2-a76f-48fa-b280-9172adc466bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognition and recall"}, {"id": "735ae25f-052e-4a5d-bf1b-05f9a651d15c", "type": "concept", "title": "Distinctiveness and association"}, {"id": "acd51e71-c2f9-4fd1-949e-3557a9ea88b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand equity and tracking"}], "description": "The gist is to understand brand metrics without reducing design to numbers alone."}, {"id": "28aaa020-2f21-4623-adb8-5f74bee4506d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design critique", "children": [{"id": "21d1e0d9-c0ff-4d80-a571-50ed8863b790", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic rationale"}, {"id": "263bea3c-a5de-4b6b-92e1-2fce5e327021", "type": "concept", "title": "Craft standards"}, {"id": "683e3ca5-eac1-4c4e-95e8-990c4bc3af07", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration logs"}], "description": "Students learn to defend work with evidence and revise without losing the idea."}]}, {"id": "c5220390-3dd9-4300-85a2-1f7a2ffc9bfa", "type": "topic", "title": "Case Studies from Leading Studios and Institutions", "description": "Case studies train taste and judgment. Students study professional identity systems to understand how strategy, craft, implementation, and public reception interact.", "children": [{"id": "9e7bcde1-ed90-4a1d-aaf9-fae72cd121f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical cases", "children": [{"id": "a0869be1-615b-4c1d-808e-d66b69dfc16c", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernist identity programs"}, {"id": "809d2a1d-bb3b-42d5-af96-29c971b2085d", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional systems"}, {"id": "9c3c32b1-e731-44c7-87ea-abf0aa71d810", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo evolution"}], "description": "Students learn from durable identity systems and the conditions that made them last."}, {"id": "ab2acb86-bdb0-4ab4-90c5-92b8ef6bf6a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary studio work", "children": [{"id": "4a92860c-3d68-4428-9022-078c179ef45e", "type": "concept", "title": "Studio research"}, {"id": "86e08705-4574-4aea-a33f-0b6e5525c661", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand launches and redesigns"}, {"id": "5eee1c78-d7ba-457f-8d76-5689f5a1c7d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio case-study structure"}], "description": "The point is to study current practice, not only canonical examples."}, {"id": "ad69a5c7-383e-449b-bdae-0c72150b231d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical comparison", "children": [{"id": "f12fb749-19fe-4073-b9c1-28957b180410", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after analysis"}, {"id": "57fcb29e-d7d3-4e32-a98d-801ee10164a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Touchpoint mapping"}, {"id": "df8d3e82-06ba-444f-af19-fefc725864bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Public critique and reception"}], "description": "Students learn to compare identity systems across purpose, context, and execution."}]}, {"id": "d207e423-5ade-4438-9776-81195258a0d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Client Presentation, Narrative, and Professional Practice", "description": "Great identity work must be explained clearly. Students learn to present strategy, concept, evidence, options, and implementation in a way clients and collaborators can understand.", "children": [{"id": "76872ac9-4da5-4e5f-8bec-6f7f06608c3c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation story", "children": [{"id": "a7494c75-167f-4598-aa25-f644a591d871", "type": "concept", "title": "Situation and insight"}, {"id": "1494d04f-8e1c-426a-8964-cd7cedb65b45", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept routes"}, {"id": "b8209549-63f4-418a-b088-0313e55f555a", "type": "concept", "title": "Final recommendation"}], "description": "Students structure a persuasive design narrative from problem to solution."}, {"id": "60ad858b-0bd6-42b2-912c-edf42daaf0b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional communication", "children": [{"id": "de8e4fe2-cacd-4aee-8b68-bd9a5e7db5b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Client language"}, {"id": "14bb335b-279f-473f-84a2-ace2a1bee3b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope and feedback management"}, {"id": "5583250e-2791-4252-ad30-b67f17004e8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Meeting and critique etiquette"}], "description": "The point is to handle critique, disagreement, and revisions with maturity."}, {"id": "f72fc71d-d458-47a3-a190-d51594601656", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio case study", "children": [{"id": "61ee65f6-4e0a-419a-b434-1532e13b44b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Process artifacts"}, {"id": "91090e22-6c2f-4688-a99b-93ae15031e12", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after and applications"}, {"id": "0662858a-4c33-45df-a4aa-0c3f69fbf397", "type": "concept", "title": "Rationale and results"}], "description": "Students document process and outcomes for internships, jobs, and senior review."}]}, {"id": "3ec10d2a-3f32-433c-9607-94c5f5416e75", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Complete Brand Identity System", "description": "The capstone integrates research, strategy, identity design, applications, guidelines, and presentation into one polished system. It should be strong enough to become a portfolio anchor.", "children": [{"id": "72da5eff-e0ea-4bfe-b897-bc9b8012fe1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategy-to-design package", "children": [{"id": "2eb87338-3793-4848-ad74-fab36bee8744", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand brief"}, {"id": "facb4a4a-3362-4e80-b809-d10c7f51e300", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative criteria"}, {"id": "668639e6-1cca-42a3-95e8-d3e0d3a34b67", "type": "concept", "title": "Design concept and rationale"}], "description": "Students connect brief, insight, concept, and system logic in one coherent deliverable."}, {"id": "bf4f5f89-6e51-43f2-9075-cd02e5349c65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complete identity system", "children": [{"id": "0f4d465e-d5c6-4145-bbba-fafd63dc68d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo suite and visual language"}, {"id": "37f58e72-2db2-45cf-a97c-cf78c10e3aa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography, color, image, and layout"}, {"id": "746dda7a-6a0b-42d3-ab39-27411b8b16ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Print, digital, social, and spatial applications"}], "description": "The point is to prove that the identity works beyond a single mark."}, {"id": "e208085a-4994-4391-9b0a-c18d901a40bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final guidelines and presentation", "children": [{"id": "96459e10-7e21-4016-9f3b-74b601450cc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand guidelines"}, {"id": "07012033-5534-45ec-bd97-be1a3d4bd1a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset library and file package"}, {"id": "f1b8fe3b-7d48-436e-8e09-d1ec8db5d861", "type": "concept", "title": "Final critique and portfolio case study"}], "description": "Students deliver the work as a professional package ready for critique or implementation."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$brndjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'branding-and-identity-design'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Branding and Identity Design',
  goal = 'Branding and Identity Design',
  summary = 'Branding and Identity Design is an advanced Year 3 studio course in logos, brand systems, and visual identity. Students learn to connect strategy, research, positioning, verbal identity, marks, typography, color, imagery, guidelines, applications, and implementation into a coherent identity system. The course is designed for graphic design students preparing for senior studio, portfolio review, internships, and professional client work. It balances strategic brand thinking with rigorous visual craft, critique, systems documentation, ethical judgment, accessibility, and real-world presentation.',
  data = $brndjson${"slug": "branding-and-identity-design", "title": "Branding and Identity Design", "description": "Branding and Identity Design is an advanced Year 3 studio course in logos, brand systems, and visual identity. Students learn to connect strategy, research, positioning, verbal identity, marks, typography, color, imagery, guidelines, applications, and implementation into a coherent identity system. The course is designed for graphic design students preparing for senior studio, portfolio review, internships, and professional client work. It balances strategic brand thinking with rigorous visual craft, critique, systems documentation, ethical judgment, accessibility, and real-world presentation.", "topics": [{"id": "114d617c-1e8e-478d-bd14-eca555f2a30a", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Strategy, Purpose, and Positioning", "description": "This opening topic frames identity design as strategic communication, not surface styling. Students learn to connect visual decisions to purpose, audience, differentiation, and organizational behavior.", "children": [{"id": "617093e8-8e55-4421-9162-f184aa0d8342", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purpose and promise", "children": [{"id": "82b63b1a-ae5d-4078-ad56-a08fc50cb977", "type": "concept", "title": "Mission, vision, and values"}, {"id": "ae0fd519-2737-4f4d-880f-a065fe380915", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand promise and proof points"}, {"id": "2f4c26f2-7948-4cac-92a1-9bf6b3882935", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder expectations"}], "description": "Students clarify what the brand exists to do and what expectation it creates for people."}, {"id": "fde34a7b-b7fb-4fd0-bc43-6f759c6b1b0d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Positioning", "children": [{"id": "a3e7ac7f-1ad8-4bf3-ae0d-a5726b2dedd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Category frame and competitors"}, {"id": "0b127225-f8d0-435b-939c-f2f5604eeef9", "type": "concept", "title": "Points of parity and difference"}, {"id": "ff505662-6325-4b5b-8beb-4950506c8d7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Positioning statements"}], "description": "The point is to define a credible place in the audience's mind before designing assets."}, {"id": "bc1652b7-bb22-44ea-bb65-3698df051ae9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative criteria", "children": [{"id": "5024ea10-0e0b-48cb-8313-b36b5527d12f", "type": "concept", "title": "Design objectives"}, {"id": "6fc30b47-5f1f-4853-9d2a-01479aaee02f", "type": "concept", "title": "Success criteria"}, {"id": "794a9c9d-08c0-4f78-ad74-99968455f853", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraints and opportunities"}], "description": "Students turn strategy into design requirements that can guide critique and revision."}]}, {"id": "04c127bc-403c-492a-83c0-032dc1ae1b9a", "type": "topic", "title": "Audience Research, Cultural Context, and Insight", "description": "This section teaches students to design from evidence and empathy. Strong identity work begins by understanding people, context, category codes, and cultural meaning.", "children": [{"id": "a6d28452-cf5d-4f64-940b-811ad5b53eae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience discovery", "children": [{"id": "2d685f8a-1d26-4d1b-ad67-43ee99d1491d", "type": "concept", "title": "Personas and need states"}, {"id": "d95d65e7-33b5-4f7a-835a-1f50390c2aa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews and observation"}, {"id": "83c847ff-77e5-4223-8bed-3852395ea37b", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience language and behavior"}], "description": "Students learn to gather useful information about the people a brand needs to serve."}, {"id": "b8915ac0-ff6f-4acc-8f11-f3c3eb4d03d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitive and category audit", "children": [{"id": "5c601996-81e7-47a7-a601-7bcbcb595d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Category conventions"}, {"id": "b64927c7-9658-4b1c-b02b-9e167e490c23", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual sameness and white space"}, {"id": "2c0c8f22-ad30-4e00-a471-de86849a38a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Benchmarking and mood boards"}], "description": "The gist is to see what already exists before deciding how to stand apart."}, {"id": "fd4ffc54-406d-4d32-b4b8-6b142c0af2ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Insight synthesis", "children": [{"id": "b851f1e4-332e-4c29-8a6f-b883b719842c", "type": "concept", "title": "Patterns and tensions"}, {"id": "e2922867-4387-4382-bb69-de05fc1855f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Design implications"}, {"id": "4f3da21c-57bb-4a13-be45-11a07a8df107", "type": "concept", "title": "Research-backed creative brief"}], "description": "Students turn messy research into focused opportunities for design action."}]}, {"id": "9b9bf243-366b-4cec-9e47-578ef9502a31", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Equity, Architecture, and Portfolio Logic", "description": "Identity systems often live inside larger brand structures. This topic introduces brand value, hierarchy, sub-brands, extensions, and portfolio clarity.", "children": [{"id": "2dfde21f-4d26-4e38-a202-3dc7457ccfe7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brand equity", "children": [{"id": "460bed79-0432-4b4c-a6e5-741046855afa", "type": "concept", "title": "Awareness and associations"}, {"id": "a13ad644-13a8-47b2-b762-f936c0bf0557", "type": "concept", "title": "Perceived quality and loyalty"}, {"id": "38ac49d5-f544-4708-9fb0-58f8af296574", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental and physical availability"}], "description": "Students learn how recognition, associations, trust, and experience create value over time."}, {"id": "778a81f3-9ea5-4526-a2fa-84823fb5b131", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Architecture models", "children": [{"id": "9586d957-ca14-4a63-97ab-e13c1911eb56", "type": "concept", "title": "Branded house"}, {"id": "3b7ab269-f122-4c08-9b91-fa143097f49e", "type": "concept", "title": "House of brands"}, {"id": "119c5b03-b622-4ba2-bbe3-0005eb4cf495", "type": "concept", "title": "Endorsed and hybrid systems"}], "description": "The point is to choose relationships that make sense to customers and organizations."}, {"id": "70ed3745-f3ad-41ae-80be-92343912760a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio decisions", "children": [{"id": "3ba8c315-635b-442c-8b74-b6dc5645a86d", "type": "concept", "title": "Product families"}, {"id": "97c6db9a-36d0-43c3-9aee-a569f035c16f", "type": "concept", "title": "Sub-brand roles"}, {"id": "c1be5b9a-c678-4a94-9bfe-433b863b61f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration and governance"}], "description": "Students consider when to extend, consolidate, rename, or separate identities."}]}, {"id": "1a370895-75c9-4f45-9fcf-67ee604c18e0", "type": "topic", "title": "Naming, Verbal Identity, Voice, and Tone", "description": "Brand identity is both visual and verbal. Students learn to shape names, taglines, message hierarchy, and tone so language and design feel like one system.", "children": [{"id": "a0e6bcff-61a0-4f3c-8dea-9272f4b9e677", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Naming strategy", "children": [{"id": "7aefeec3-17d7-496e-89cd-225cb6bc1aab", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, evocative, coined, and founder names"}, {"id": "d6b7b236-947f-4959-933f-168305e924c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening and shortlisting"}, {"id": "1125fab8-6003-401e-8bda-a19c71e234b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Trademark and domain awareness"}], "description": "The point is to generate names that are memorable, usable, ownable, and strategically aligned."}, {"id": "6537988f-1021-4e7e-8a86-6834285c4b15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voice and tone", "children": [{"id": "387b578e-f6be-4d2d-8379-816ec27f9fad", "type": "concept", "title": "Personality attributes"}, {"id": "154860c2-eb43-4239-a793-820d330ea9de", "type": "concept", "title": "Tone range by context"}, {"id": "f78f2e8e-e693-4c69-b14c-305b47d76d0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Do and do not examples"}], "description": "Students define how the brand sounds in different situations without becoming inconsistent."}, {"id": "065cbeb2-cba1-4c99-b016-fb9d9ff58c90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Messaging system", "children": [{"id": "eb48acc0-8b49-4cd0-a295-16dc00542201", "type": "concept", "title": "Taglines and value propositions"}, {"id": "e41fd282-83d2-4a96-9fe1-3f54866f5044", "type": "concept", "title": "Message pillars"}, {"id": "3829757e-8b91-4a3e-a5be-6625c995382d", "type": "concept", "title": "Proof points and calls to action"}], "description": "Students learn to structure claims and stories for multiple audiences and channels."}]}, {"id": "a586efba-dff3-4722-a31d-e779632b68c4", "type": "topic", "title": "Logo Design, Marks, Wordmarks, and Symbol Systems", "description": "This studio core develops disciplined mark-making. Students move from sketches to refined logos that are distinctive, scalable, flexible, and strategically justified.", "children": [{"id": "c7e2c172-7aec-4208-9ab5-3a62e6ed515c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept development", "children": [{"id": "0d31d479-f83a-4396-b5ed-60c6110c671d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sketching and ideation"}, {"id": "4486b7e8-1d8a-4a96-8091-b5948a5d1d2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Metaphor and abstraction"}, {"id": "c71c602f-20eb-4eea-954a-0eaacad5e9c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept selection criteria"}], "description": "Students learn to generate many routes before committing to one polished direction."}, {"id": "badaf466-b963-479f-92b0-54f3fa1227e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logo construction", "children": [{"id": "dfd6aaef-3869-4878-8616-999091062304", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometry and optical correction"}, {"id": "262b4b85-dddf-4483-9465-38a2a4bc0c3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative space"}, {"id": "5b834345-fe69-4b01-8433-b68cee2e9f97", "type": "concept", "title": "Lockups and clear space"}], "description": "The gist is to refine form so the mark works technically and perceptually."}, {"id": "4b53f474-aa27-46b1-93a4-1b53f09b1a19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing and refinement", "children": [{"id": "d4a13058-63d9-4b34-9b5b-9fdfc108e4f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-size performance"}, {"id": "473195a0-6f3d-478d-8c45-0c031db670f8", "type": "concept", "title": "One-color and reverse use"}, {"id": "64e3678f-ba44-41e4-80f2-290282ed75a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Confusability and memorability"}], "description": "Students learn to stress-test marks before finalizing them."}]}, {"id": "00bc6dc8-149e-426a-9da1-cb5b48dfe0da", "type": "topic", "title": "Typography for Identity Systems", "description": "Typography carries personality, hierarchy, and usability. This topic teaches students to choose and use type as a strategic brand voice across print and digital contexts.", "children": [{"id": "b00fcc47-2e64-48ae-95e6-9c6265ec433b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Typeface selection", "children": [{"id": "dd4038a1-2d8e-43de-9bfa-4dee2376ebf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Classification and personality"}, {"id": "157bc803-2087-4fcf-89b3-01c616977ffb", "type": "concept", "title": "Licensing and availability"}, {"id": "e5529add-0b96-4d45-bfe9-e25bc65e05d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Variable fonts and digital use"}], "description": "Students learn to match type choices to strategy, audience, and implementation reality."}, {"id": "522e7d4b-c9dd-4dea-abca-70bf689416ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Typographic system", "children": [{"id": "c0577c32-7edf-414f-81f9-3382ef775ed0", "type": "concept", "title": "Display, text, and UI roles"}, {"id": "f32760d1-13a8-4755-8824-827d512752a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale, spacing, and grids"}, {"id": "64893252-ae01-4952-b3fe-879734e1006b", "type": "concept", "title": "Language support and accessibility"}], "description": "The point is to create hierarchy and rhythm that can scale across many assets."}, {"id": "9bd9f9d3-bce8-4fee-bfa7-228c8f745832", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Custom type and lettering", "children": [{"id": "9a31de74-931d-44ca-b0fa-a3ddf5bf60ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Letterform refinement"}, {"id": "8d9cb9c4-4cef-4b6c-950f-79ee65445301", "type": "concept", "title": "Optical balance"}, {"id": "a2ffb352-4d7f-4997-8d5e-c7f2c7ff1160", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency with the broader system"}], "description": "Students explore when a custom wordmark or type modification is worth the effort."}]}, {"id": "872eb134-a700-47b7-9763-7697e26e9e03", "type": "topic", "title": "Color, Form, Image, and Graphic Language", "description": "A brand becomes recognizable through repeated visual behavior. Students build palettes, forms, imagery, icons, patterns, and compositional rules that support a coherent identity.", "children": [{"id": "6b9c67bb-59ea-4e6a-aa7f-3b261f54d7dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color systems", "children": [{"id": "e882f3b1-e1ee-4292-887e-b91537037901", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary palettes"}, {"id": "e19ccf2c-b7a6-4df7-a352-88644f5b90af", "type": "concept", "title": "CMYK, RGB, HEX, Pantone, and accessibility"}, {"id": "a6f004d6-17cf-4f34-8564-6e5824ab9432", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and color roles"}], "description": "Students learn to make palettes that are expressive, accessible, and reproducible."}, {"id": "79244f38-7573-40f7-a5f4-3935de47364d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Graphic elements", "children": [{"id": "7893b07a-0e61-4a1a-a35a-eacec872b3cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Patterns and shapes"}, {"id": "f75c7dcf-6f11-41ab-9b2d-5bb4e3486a33", "type": "concept", "title": "Icon and illustration styles"}, {"id": "37d3c170-de81-4037-88cf-1637c375fa12", "type": "concept", "title": "Photography and art direction"}], "description": "The point is to create useful design ingredients beyond the logo."}, {"id": "43ad39e2-fa87-45ae-902b-21e50dbc6ff2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual consistency", "children": [{"id": "260b789c-1461-4671-895b-68b6dfc9a02d", "type": "concept", "title": "Motifs and signature moves"}, {"id": "ef498e18-41fc-4860-90a9-f22ab2d7a412", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules for variation"}, {"id": "1ce80ca3-fca5-42ac-aff7-a1d4da20e5a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding sameness and clutter"}], "description": "Students learn how repetition and variation create a living system."}]}, {"id": "9a8f8697-c7d5-459e-9a96-5161277d89ee", "type": "topic", "title": "Identity Systems, Grid Logic, and Design Principles", "description": "This topic shifts students from individual deliverables to systems thinking. A strong identity creates rules that other designers can use without weakening the brand.", "children": [{"id": "d4f352db-d1d2-4a01-b7bc-153f0d54cc74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "System principles", "children": [{"id": "95de0735-1d0d-4086-8ef8-11ace8e25349", "type": "concept", "title": "Core design principles"}, {"id": "6088aaf6-e852-4138-a134-7b7a2997502a", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible versus fixed elements"}, {"id": "ad721b06-8fe8-4bb8-bde1-eba9ceb39fc2", "type": "concept", "title": "System boundaries"}], "description": "Students identify the few rules that make the identity recognizable."}, {"id": "6241c5da-c9ff-4317-be2d-6e5667ab6eba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layout and grid logic", "children": [{"id": "dfd75409-3311-4d45-baf1-b4db97b71571", "type": "concept", "title": "Grid structures"}, {"id": "60d64b77-3d84-47e1-8f4c-2b05bba369f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Spacing and proportion"}, {"id": "1e4c162a-49b5-4fc3-8205-eae157ac0929", "type": "concept", "title": "Modular layouts"}], "description": "The gist is to make applications feel related even across different formats."}, {"id": "925681d6-0736-4be9-a83b-a69cb1d9347d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scalability", "children": [{"id": "3311689a-fd1b-4aaa-a750-d30eaa0eba47", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset families"}, {"id": "fe257c50-24f5-4871-b6fe-a06768e11246", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates and variants"}, {"id": "824172d9-7142-44a3-97e1-febc77684670", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth without fragmentation"}], "description": "Students learn to design for both small assets and complex campaigns."}]}, {"id": "fdb7a787-78ee-4529-8f69-d725102fb469", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Applications Across Touchpoints", "description": "Identity design becomes real through use. Students apply the system across varied touchpoints and learn to adjust while preserving recognizability.", "children": [{"id": "d856abcc-c877-49c9-9623-5ff984c0908d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Print and packaging", "children": [{"id": "d24226b6-2833-4c64-82a0-4ed2c4049453", "type": "concept", "title": "Stationery and collateral"}, {"id": "57421bfa-beb8-471f-bd72-7e8de394a893", "type": "concept", "title": "Packaging hierarchy"}, {"id": "cebbdf86-9233-48ce-af60-b24144d2953d", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials, finishes, and print constraints"}], "description": "Students practice translating identity into tangible, production-aware formats."}, {"id": "3f191904-3b14-445f-8436-5ff49042ecb2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital and social", "children": [{"id": "80cd95f7-05d7-42f2-a7d5-08a6087bec9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Social templates"}, {"id": "fe48757e-7a16-4857-8536-a9bab7e9dc07", "type": "concept", "title": "Web and mobile assets"}, {"id": "2be07a82-4ffe-4ae6-81bb-20885a71f235", "type": "concept", "title": "Thumbnails, avatars, and responsive marks"}], "description": "The point is to create brand behavior for fast-moving, screen-based contexts."}, {"id": "0416aeac-9c44-44f8-8334-700ff029901d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spatial and experiential", "children": [{"id": "43cc0e25-0a10-4bfe-963e-2e131d080803", "type": "concept", "title": "Signage and wayfinding"}, {"id": "42b996f7-116e-45a9-896f-6faa7d02e7b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Events and retail"}, {"id": "0d5a439f-98e8-4e3c-965c-d770e7d358ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental graphics"}], "description": "Students consider how identity functions in environments and public interactions."}]}, {"id": "ba2dd522-f3f3-43f8-a298-60c0a2e234b3", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Brand Systems, UI Components, and Accessibility", "description": "Modern identities must work inside interfaces and design systems. Students learn how brand choices become tokens, components, states, and accessible experiences.", "children": [{"id": "706c5358-1fae-4980-a5bf-84e8da32d9a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design tokens", "children": [{"id": "a7127c51-7ce8-42e8-94f3-23ef20ceae0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Color tokens"}, {"id": "6ad56203-5591-4c4d-ae4c-01c783703b20", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography tokens"}, {"id": "c10ec19b-194f-495c-b8db-b674fd3c01f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Spacing, radius, and elevation rules"}], "description": "Students translate brand choices into maintainable digital variables."}, {"id": "adb8dffc-6a13-4687-8a81-bdb93cba1501", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UI components", "children": [{"id": "37544481-c2c8-4822-ad23-4086cacf7ca5", "type": "concept", "title": "Buttons, forms, cards, and navigation"}, {"id": "5b0f0e7d-2450-4bc5-b771-c7e833349c30", "type": "concept", "title": "States and feedback"}, {"id": "820243a3-1730-4cd8-825e-842d0fbcd92b", "type": "concept", "title": "Component documentation"}], "description": "The point is to preserve brand expression while supporting usability."}, {"id": "e5aeadba-d525-4089-991c-09e75604f3be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility", "children": [{"id": "faea7fb3-fe7f-4d73-b263-9275c42c8f80", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and color blindness"}, {"id": "a9786468-f263-428b-8437-5581b196aea5", "type": "concept", "title": "Readable type and motion sensitivity"}, {"id": "893f066c-a9f1-4391-92aa-e8d5f427fa38", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and semantic handoff"}], "description": "Students learn that brand consistency cannot override legibility, contrast, or inclusive use."}]}, {"id": "6a563e2c-046b-4940-8267-0371dea6c5ab", "type": "topic", "title": "Motion, Sound, and Experiential Brand Behavior", "description": "Identity increasingly lives in time. This topic introduces motion, interaction, and sensory behavior as part of the brand system.", "children": [{"id": "739e7946-1940-4375-adfc-e0ed309e0000", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motion principles", "children": [{"id": "2f28d55b-c9ef-4291-9379-f1717d7ae4cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Timing and easing"}, {"id": "2f2f9c46-5832-4dbb-a18f-8e8b7bc95c2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions and reveals"}, {"id": "7f007148-f158-4b6b-830e-bea5374c032c", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion personality"}], "description": "Students define how a brand moves so animation supports identity rather than decoration."}, {"id": "4635d434-415e-4db9-9ca5-181828c5647c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interactive behavior", "children": [{"id": "974b8395-463d-4723-82d5-245d3cf3599f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hover, tap, loading, and feedback states"}, {"id": "b336d449-7ee6-4f38-b6f7-2c93361d1c3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Microinteractions"}, {"id": "af875f28-9905-45b0-b986-b241722973df", "type": "concept", "title": "Error and success moments"}], "description": "The gist is to make brand expression responsive to user action."}, {"id": "fbaae073-8b29-4121-80a4-8ad2bcf0968d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensory extensions", "children": [{"id": "c232d113-f96a-4ded-acbb-da6d0e61d10d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sonic logos and cues"}, {"id": "8b845924-2f0d-4255-9db8-10d4c9c72869", "type": "concept", "title": "Event experience"}, {"id": "28bcf86d-1b67-4693-b746-fb2bf55c3c39", "type": "concept", "title": "Multisensory consistency"}], "description": "Students consider sound, haptics, and experience design where appropriate."}]}, {"id": "d136ea02-b4ea-475f-9259-ba27a43061b1", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Guidelines, Asset Libraries, and Governance", "description": "Guidelines turn design into implementation. Students learn to document rules, rationale, files, and examples so a brand can be used by many people without falling apart.", "children": [{"id": "68ae7928-aea6-4188-9538-fe49fa5f2f93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Guideline structure", "children": [{"id": "e0dbfc83-914a-4790-a7b2-b1c4b98c3f5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo rules"}, {"id": "9cd3c432-4a98-43af-b69f-7b708a8955fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, type, image, and layout standards"}, {"id": "fb9d9a54-2ddf-40e6-bbec-ea00182c1cbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice, examples, and rationale"}], "description": "Students learn what a useful brand guide must explain."}, {"id": "be3fbc0d-1a96-4b92-a5e5-de22f0dcb1be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Asset management", "children": [{"id": "700e79e0-a02f-462c-8f37-4b9b8236cd6d", "type": "concept", "title": "File formats and naming"}, {"id": "ba1e0bc3-8aa2-4798-a6e6-7557dda2de83", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates and libraries"}, {"id": "de03e424-1657-451c-a63c-f2abdcedc952", "type": "concept", "title": "Version control"}], "description": "The point is to package files so teams can actually use them correctly."}, {"id": "bb5eb2ba-9ef3-42a6-bb80-2d472297a5ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance", "children": [{"id": "4a1cc187-5351-4a4c-91f3-823979c3595a", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval workflows"}, {"id": "bad6063f-981d-4104-97f1-5ae0703a597a", "type": "concept", "title": "Use cases and exceptions"}, {"id": "d6ea9161-c9be-4736-b6a9-5f280802c264", "type": "concept", "title": "Training and stewardship"}], "description": "Students consider how brands are maintained after launch."}]}, {"id": "bdd2a980-ecfa-4d64-aac0-8f7b7b1b0fd4", "type": "topic", "title": "Rebranding, Refreshes, and Identity Migration", "description": "Rebranding is not a blank slate. Students learn to preserve useful equity, diagnose real problems, and manage change across audiences and touchpoints.", "children": [{"id": "67cb9ff3-eea7-4b24-ac3f-765b5b8897c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brand audit", "children": [{"id": "be0c7acc-46ae-4f6d-b02a-493d2a506071", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity inventory"}, {"id": "ee9b2c59-02aa-477e-ba1a-d3e2e1403983", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder interviews"}, {"id": "91e89594-b0a9-4a67-8d4f-fdeb8cde217e", "type": "concept", "title": "Touchpoint and consistency audit"}], "description": "Students evaluate what should be kept, repaired, retired, or amplified."}, {"id": "96286f26-8a87-4c4e-a35b-b3a195c68444", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Redesign strategy", "children": [{"id": "fe0c1adc-57a9-43b4-afa6-b4ab768257fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Refresh versus rebrand"}, {"id": "c8012d39-0426-4c65-b170-93dfeda7a2a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration risk"}, {"id": "5187a235-a128-4c40-9bee-33a15e69473f", "type": "concept", "title": "Launch narrative"}], "description": "The gist is to decide the degree of change before changing the visuals."}, {"id": "d386d1b2-eddd-49c6-80de-159474fe97d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation planning", "children": [{"id": "fe3d2a43-2d65-4b54-8dc1-c932b8e6b91f", "type": "concept", "title": "Phased rollout"}, {"id": "976353ba-bf1b-498e-b8fd-469f6871c2a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Old-to-new asset mapping"}, {"id": "c9a8e61b-7f2b-4dcd-96ae-1494c8fbcf51", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal adoption and training"}], "description": "Students learn how a redesign rolls out in the real world."}]}, {"id": "fded4907-249c-4a99-b179-6dd19ecbec7a", "type": "topic", "title": "Global, Local, Inclusive, and Ethical Branding", "description": "This topic asks students to design with cultural intelligence and responsibility. Identity work can include, exclude, inspire, confuse, stereotype, or repair trust.", "children": [{"id": "4dc933a5-d76e-4a55-a431-59a613b9e527", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural meaning", "children": [{"id": "3927abbb-9f5a-4e20-8340-d14097af91b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Localization and translation"}, {"id": "5b6d2934-863d-4bc6-8be7-bd2797f57920", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural codes and taboos"}, {"id": "b3fa1ed7-e920-4827-aaa6-86634d834ee0", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding appropriation and stereotypes"}], "description": "Students learn to research symbols, colors, language, and imagery across contexts."}, {"id": "12a6b64e-8f73-4118-9398-3cb2cffa212d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive identity", "children": [{"id": "8ac9b265-4425-44b0-9e04-d55420ca27b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and imagery"}, {"id": "a42c6bfe-a814-4e33-8759-95ea04ad4765", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility as identity quality"}, {"id": "9463d3d1-58ce-405e-8b73-727b68ea1896", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive naming and language"}], "description": "The point is to consider who is represented, who can use the system, and who may be harmed."}, {"id": "43bfb301-ed42-405e-90a2-e1904eb4ff32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical practice", "children": [{"id": "e8010bef-abaa-4568-9b87-6b7a294384ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Greenwashing and authenticity"}, {"id": "bffd38fc-a717-458f-ae17-233cfd31f4fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Dark patterns and manipulation"}, {"id": "e13b7d28-3300-4ec6-816d-6448dfcfebc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency and accountability"}], "description": "Students connect design choices to social, environmental, and reputational consequences."}]}, {"id": "7046f2b4-1555-444f-bcb6-8de247c86645", "type": "topic", "title": "Brand Measurement, Testing, and Critique", "description": "Identity systems should be judged by more than taste. Students learn to evaluate recognition, clarity, usability, distinctiveness, fit, and audience response.", "children": [{"id": "de03487c-0170-4f79-a617-66ad9d6f64fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Qualitative testing", "children": [{"id": "50e7370d-0dda-4178-a5ef-c6d79c2baedc", "type": "concept", "title": "Perception interviews"}, {"id": "cfea8f3e-9c4b-4205-b46e-a707001b8497", "type": "concept", "title": "Preference versus fit"}, {"id": "65822adc-d14c-4ae3-ba57-7d5c901f50fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique protocols"}], "description": "Students use critique and user feedback to identify strengths and problems."}, {"id": "cbc68ef3-6fdf-4f69-b50c-b30ab77ccb66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quantitative indicators", "children": [{"id": "65f581e2-a76f-48fa-b280-9172adc466bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognition and recall"}, {"id": "735ae25f-052e-4a5d-bf1b-05f9a651d15c", "type": "concept", "title": "Distinctiveness and association"}, {"id": "acd51e71-c2f9-4fd1-949e-3557a9ea88b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand equity and tracking"}], "description": "The gist is to understand brand metrics without reducing design to numbers alone."}, {"id": "28aaa020-2f21-4623-adb8-5f74bee4506d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design critique", "children": [{"id": "21d1e0d9-c0ff-4d80-a571-50ed8863b790", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic rationale"}, {"id": "263bea3c-a5de-4b6b-92e1-2fce5e327021", "type": "concept", "title": "Craft standards"}, {"id": "683e3ca5-eac1-4c4e-95e8-990c4bc3af07", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration logs"}], "description": "Students learn to defend work with evidence and revise without losing the idea."}]}, {"id": "c5220390-3dd9-4300-85a2-1f7a2ffc9bfa", "type": "topic", "title": "Case Studies from Leading Studios and Institutions", "description": "Case studies train taste and judgment. Students study professional identity systems to understand how strategy, craft, implementation, and public reception interact.", "children": [{"id": "9e7bcde1-ed90-4a1d-aaf9-fae72cd121f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical cases", "children": [{"id": "a0869be1-615b-4c1d-808e-d66b69dfc16c", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernist identity programs"}, {"id": "809d2a1d-bb3b-42d5-af96-29c971b2085d", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional systems"}, {"id": "9c3c32b1-e731-44c7-87ea-abf0aa71d810", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo evolution"}], "description": "Students learn from durable identity systems and the conditions that made them last."}, {"id": "ab2acb86-bdb0-4ab4-90c5-92b8ef6bf6a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary studio work", "children": [{"id": "4a92860c-3d68-4428-9022-078c179ef45e", "type": "concept", "title": "Studio research"}, {"id": "86e08705-4574-4aea-a33f-0b6e5525c661", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand launches and redesigns"}, {"id": "5eee1c78-d7ba-457f-8d76-5689f5a1c7d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio case-study structure"}], "description": "The point is to study current practice, not only canonical examples."}, {"id": "ad69a5c7-383e-449b-bdae-0c72150b231d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical comparison", "children": [{"id": "f12fb749-19fe-4073-b9c1-28957b180410", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after analysis"}, {"id": "57fcb29e-d7d3-4e32-a98d-801ee10164a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Touchpoint mapping"}, {"id": "df8d3e82-06ba-444f-af19-fefc725864bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Public critique and reception"}], "description": "Students learn to compare identity systems across purpose, context, and execution."}]}, {"id": "d207e423-5ade-4438-9776-81195258a0d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Client Presentation, Narrative, and Professional Practice", "description": "Great identity work must be explained clearly. Students learn to present strategy, concept, evidence, options, and implementation in a way clients and collaborators can understand.", "children": [{"id": "76872ac9-4da5-4e5f-8bec-6f7f06608c3c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation story", "children": [{"id": "a7494c75-167f-4598-aa25-f644a591d871", "type": "concept", "title": "Situation and insight"}, {"id": "1494d04f-8e1c-426a-8964-cd7cedb65b45", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept routes"}, {"id": "b8209549-63f4-418a-b088-0313e55f555a", "type": "concept", "title": "Final recommendation"}], "description": "Students structure a persuasive design narrative from problem to solution."}, {"id": "60ad858b-0bd6-42b2-912c-edf42daaf0b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional communication", "children": [{"id": "de8e4fe2-cacd-4aee-8b68-bd9a5e7db5b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Client language"}, {"id": "14bb335b-279f-473f-84a2-ace2a1bee3b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope and feedback management"}, {"id": "5583250e-2791-4252-ad30-b67f17004e8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Meeting and critique etiquette"}], "description": "The point is to handle critique, disagreement, and revisions with maturity."}, {"id": "f72fc71d-d458-47a3-a190-d51594601656", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio case study", "children": [{"id": "61ee65f6-4e0a-419a-b434-1532e13b44b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Process artifacts"}, {"id": "91090e22-6c2f-4688-a99b-93ae15031e12", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after and applications"}, {"id": "0662858a-4c33-45df-a4aa-0c3f69fbf397", "type": "concept", "title": "Rationale and results"}], "description": "Students document process and outcomes for internships, jobs, and senior review."}]}, {"id": "3ec10d2a-3f32-433c-9607-94c5f5416e75", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Complete Brand Identity System", "description": "The capstone integrates research, strategy, identity design, applications, guidelines, and presentation into one polished system. It should be strong enough to become a portfolio anchor.", "children": [{"id": "72da5eff-e0ea-4bfe-b897-bc9b8012fe1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategy-to-design package", "children": [{"id": "2eb87338-3793-4848-ad74-fab36bee8744", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand brief"}, {"id": "facb4a4a-3362-4e80-b809-d10c7f51e300", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative criteria"}, {"id": "668639e6-1cca-42a3-95e8-d3e0d3a34b67", "type": "concept", "title": "Design concept and rationale"}], "description": "Students connect brief, insight, concept, and system logic in one coherent deliverable."}, {"id": "bf4f5f89-6e51-43f2-9075-cd02e5349c65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complete identity system", "children": [{"id": "0f4d465e-d5c6-4145-bbba-fafd63dc68d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Logo suite and visual language"}, {"id": "37f58e72-2db2-45cf-a97c-cf78c10e3aa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography, color, image, and layout"}, {"id": "746dda7a-6a0b-42d3-ab39-27411b8b16ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Print, digital, social, and spatial applications"}], "description": "The point is to prove that the identity works beyond a single mark."}, {"id": "e208085a-4994-4391-9b0a-c18d901a40bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final guidelines and presentation", "children": [{"id": "96459e10-7e21-4016-9f3b-74b601450cc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand guidelines"}, {"id": "07012033-5534-45ec-bd97-be1a3d4bd1a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset library and file package"}, {"id": "f1b8fe3b-7d48-436e-8e09-d1ec8db5d861", "type": "concept", "title": "Final critique and portfolio case study"}], "description": "Students deliver the work as a professional package ready for critique or implementation."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$brndjson$::jsonb,
